cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  AURA — Asymmetric Paired-Annotation Learning for Multi-Structure ULF
  Pediatric Brain MRI Segmentation
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the challenge report and nnU-Net.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/minhdang050806/LISA-2026-Challenge-Report-A-nnU-Net-based-asymmetric-supervision-strategy
abstract: >-
  Official code release for the LISA 2026 Challenge (Task 2) report. AURA is an
  nnU-Net-based asymmetric supervision strategy for ultra-low-field pediatric
  brain MRI segmentation. It anchors training to the high-field-derived
  annotation that the challenge scores, and admits the low-field-edited
  annotation only through a bounded reliability gate driven by label
  disagreement, anatomical boundaries, predictive uncertainty, class-specific
  reliability, and training stage. The paired annotations are used only during
  training; at inference the models require nothing but the ULF MRI.
keywords:
  - ultra-low-field MRI
  - pediatric brain segmentation
  - asymmetric supervision
  - label noise
  - nnU-Net
  - LISA 2026
